# Frobenius push-forward and pull-back on degree-zero Picard groups

Definition: `AlgebraicCurve_FrobeniusEndoPic0` (`16d9c6d9-b503-56b5-aa8d-f254c7635f7b`), by Claude,
2026-09-05.

The standing setting is a field $K$, a field $F$ with a $K$-algebra structure, a natural number
$\ell$ and a $K$-algebra endomorphism $\varphi : F \to F$ satisfying `IsFrobeniusEndo ℓ φ`, i.e.
every $x \in F$ has some $y$ with $\varphi(y) = x^{\ell}$ and every $y \in F$ has some $x$ with
$\varphi(y) = x^{\ell}$ (so the image of $\varphi$ is exactly the set of $\ell$-th powers);
`frobNorm` picks, for each $f$, a witness with $\varphi(\mathrm{frobNorm}(f)) = f^{\ell}$. Sections
further assume $\ell$ prime, $\mathrm{char}\,F = \ell$, and `HasPrincipalDivisors K F` where needed.

The place calculus records that, for $\ell \neq 0$ and $\varphi$ integral, restriction of places
along $\varphi$ is injective (so each fibre `fiberAlong` is a singleton), that the ramification
index along $\varphi$ — the infimum of the positive values $\mathrm{ord}_w(\varphi f)$, $f \neq 0$ —
equals $\ell$ at every place, that $\mathrm{ord}_{w|_\varphi}(\mathrm{frobNorm}(f)) =
\mathrm{ord}_w(f)$, and that the algebra norm of $F$ over itself along $\varphi$ agrees with
`frobNorm` when the degree `finrankAlong K φ` equals $\ell$. From these follow the two predicates
that the divisor machinery requires: `normFormulaAlong` (the push-forward of the divisor of $f$ is
the divisor of its norm) under integrality, module-finiteness, degree $\ell$, surjectivity of place
restriction and all inertia degrees equal to $1$; and `fundamentalIdentityAlong`, obtained from
$\sum_{w \mid v} e_w f_w = \ell$ over the one-element fibres.

The two main definitions are the induced endomorphisms of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(K,F)$.
`frobeniusPushforwardDegZero` restricts `Divisor.pushforwardAlong φ` to degree-zero divisors, and
`pushforwardPic0` is the map it induces on the quotient by principal divisors, principality being
preserved by the norm formula. Dually, `frobeniusPullbackDegZero` restricts `Divisor.pullbackAlong
φ` (degree zero being preserved by the fundamental identity), and `pullbackPic0` is the induced map
on $\mathrm{Pic}^0$. Compatibility lemmas identify both maps on classes `Pic0.mk D`, and
`isPrincipal_pushforwardAlong` states preservation of principality directly.

**Relation to Mathlib.** The `Place`, `Divisor` and `Pic0` framework used here, together with the
predicates `IsFrobeniusEndo`, `NormFormulaAlong` and `FundamentalIdentityAlong`, is the project's
own; only the underlying valuation-subring, norm and quotient-group material is Mathlib's. The
auxiliary lemma [`ValuationSubring.pow_mem_iff`](../def/AlgebraicCurve_FrobeniusEndoPic0.html#L13),
stating that $x^n \in A$ iff $x \in A$ for a valuation subring $A$ and $n \neq 0$, is placed in
Mathlib's root namespace.

**Where it is used.** These two operators on the degree-zero Picard group of a function field in
characteristic $\ell$ are the geometric Frobenius and its transpose on the Jacobian of a modular
curve in characteristic $\ell$; their sum is the shape of the Eichler–Shimura relation used to
compare Hecke operators with Frobenius in the study of the Galois representations attached to
modular forms.

